description: "Prevent premature completion claims"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Definition of Done

Do not report a task as complete until all applicable checks are satisfied.

Required sequence:

1. Requested behavior implemented.
2. Regression tests added for newly fixed defects.
3. Targeted tests pass.
4. Existing nearby regressions pass.
5. Ruff format passes.
6. Ruff check passes.
7. mypy passes.
8. AI contract tests pass when applicable.
9. Full pytest passes.
10. GitHub Quality Gate passes when a PR exists.
11. No unresolved known P1/P2 review finding applies to the current HEAD.
12. No prohibited live external calls occurred.
13. Requested scope boundaries remain intact.

Always report the exact commit SHA that was validated.

Never use results from an older commit as evidence for the current HEAD.

Never say "all checks pass" while GitHub Actions is still running.

Never merge unless explicitly instructed by the user.
